3.5. Mobility process for outgoing students 

3.5.1. Eligibility and participation: 
1) Subject to specific requirements of each program, all students may apply 
to participate in Mobility programs; 
2) An Outgoing Student studying on Academic Exchange (for the period of 
1-2 semesters)  should be registered by OR to a placeholder course.  Financial 
obligations on tuition fees and stipend provisions are regulated by the internal 
documents of NU; 
3) In cases when selection for Student mobility is competitive,  student 
applications are reviewed by the School Selection Committee; 
4) To be eligible to participate in an outgoing Academic Mobility, a student 
must: 
be currently enrolled at NU as a degree -seeking student , ensuring his/her 
studying at NU to be completed within 4 (four) years; 
must have completed at least one academic year at NU  (for undergraduate 
students) and at least one semester at NU (for graduate students); 
an applicant must be in good standing during the whole period of studying at 
NU (i.e. not on probation or with conditional status, should not have any academic 
or/and disciplinary sanctions imposed); 
have a CGPA of 3.0 and above (does not apply to programs with no GPA);  
have no incomplete grades in any courses; 
be 18 years old on the day of application to the Mobility program; 
5) Evaluation of applications is based on: 
academic merit; 
academic and research reference, statement of purpose, and interview;  
where relevant, a priority shall be given to students without academic mobility 
experience (if previous and current programs are funded by NU);  
other relevant criteria, such as language skills, and social and community 
commitment, where applicable; 
Eligibility and requirements for each kind of program will be announced by 
means of emails and/or posted on the web page of respective NU Schools. 
3.5.2. Application process: 
Applicants for outgoing Student mobility must submit to the appropriate 
School Selection Committee the following application materials:  
a copy of passport; 
a copy of the transcript; 
a person al statement indicating the motivation and expected benefits of 
participating in Academic mobility;

